---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
const updated = "November 15, 2026";
---

<Layout title="Terms of Use — Resolvd" description="Terms for using the resolvd.dev website. The Resolvd software itself is governed by the FSL-1.1 license.">
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-20 pb-10 md:pt-28">
      <span class="mb-6 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface)] px-3 py-1 text-xs text-[var(--color-fg-muted)]">
        <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-brand)] shadow-[0_0_8px_var(--color-brand)]"></span>
        Legal
      </span>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-[1.05]">
        Terms of <span class="text-[var(--color-brand)]">use</span>.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-[var(--color-fg-muted)] leading-relaxed">
        These terms cover this website. The Resolvd software has its own license.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-[var(--color-fg-dim)]">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="legal mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pb-16">
      <p>
        These Terms of Use ("Terms") govern your use of resolvd.dev, published by Hearne Technologies ("we," "us"). By using this site, you agree to these Terms. If you don't agree, please don't use the site.
      </p>

      <h2>The software is licensed separately</h2>
      <p>
        Resolvd is source-available under the <a href="/license/">Functional Source License (FSL-1.1-Apache-2.0)</a>. Your rights to use, modify, self-host and redistribute the software come from that license, not from these Terms. If anything here conflicts with the license, the license controls for the software.
      </p>
      <p>
        There is no hosted Resolvd service and no paid plan. If you install Resolvd, you run it on your own infrastructure and are responsible for operating, securing, backing up and updating it.
      </p>

      <h2>Using the site</h2>
      <p>You may use this site for lawful purposes: to learn about Resolvd, read the documentation and get the software. You agree not to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Misuse the site, interfere with its operation, or try to access it in ways we didn't intend.</li>
        <li>Probe, scan or test the site's security without our written permission. Security issues in the Resolvd software can be reported through the GitHub repository.</li>
        <li>Pass off this site, its content or the Resolvd name as your own, or imply we endorse you.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Documentation and content</h2>
      <p>
        Documentation, guides, install snippets and release notes are provided to help you run Resolvd. You may quote, link to and adapt them for operating your own installation. The site's design, the Resolvd name and logo, and the Hearne Technologies name and logo are ours. Please don't reuse the branding in ways that suggest an official connection.
      </p>
      <p>
        Third-party names that appear on this site, such as Action1, Zabbix, Uptime Kuma, Microsoft, Google, Slack and PagerDuty, are trademarks of their owners and are used only to describe compatibility. Their use doesn't imply affiliation or endorsement.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>
        This site links to GitHub and other third-party sites we don't control. We aren't responsible for their content, terms or privacy practices.
      </p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        This website and its content are provided "as is" and "as available." We work to keep the documentation accurate for each release, but we don't warrant that the site or its content is error-free, complete or current, or that following it will produce a particular result on your systems. Test changes before running them in production.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, Hearne Technologies won't be liable for any indirect, incidental, special or consequential damages, including lost data or downtime, arising from your use of, or inability to use, this website or its content. Nothing in these Terms limits liability that can't be limited under applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms as the site or the law changes. When we do, we'll revise the "Last updated" date above. Continuing to use the site after a change means you accept the updated Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of Texas, USA, without regard to its conflict-of-laws rules. Disputes relating to this website will be handled in the state or federal courts located in Texas.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these Terms? Email <a href="mailto:support@hearnetech.com">support@hearnetech.com</a>. Hearne Technologies, Lufkin, Texas. See also our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style is:global>
  .legal { font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--color-fg-muted); }
  .legal h2 { margin-top: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: var(--color-fg-strong); }
  .legal p { margin-top: 0.9rem; }
  .legal ul { margin-top: 0.9rem; padding-left: 1.25rem; list-style: disc; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .legal li::marker { color: var(--color-brand); }
  .legal strong { color: var(--color-fg-strong); font-weight: 600; }
  .legal a { color: var(--color-brand); }
  .legal a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
